{"The event listener in AdminPermissions.registerListener() wraps all cleanup logic in Profile.isFeatureEnabled(Profile.Feature.ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ) (V1), but ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ_V2 does NOT depend on V1, so when only V2 is enabled, client deletion leaves orphaned authorization resources": 0.8279242515563965, "ClientPermissionsV2 uses resourceServer.getId() as the ResourceStore ownerId when looking up resources, but resources are created/owned by resourceServer.getClientId(), so lookups fail and client/all-clients scope checks can incorrectly deny access": 0.5895869135856628, "In ClientPermissionsV2.hasPermission(ClientModel, String), when no specific resource exists for the client, getResourceTypeResource() can return null which is passed directly to findByResource(server, resource), causing a NullPointerException": 0.9313532114028931, "In ClientPermissionsV2.hasPermission(ClientModel, String), the loop over evaluated permissions does not filter by permission.getResourceId().equals(resource.getId()), unlike UserPermissionsV2.hasPermission(), which could cause incorrect permission grants when falling back to all-clients resource": 0.4918360412120819, "The private method getEvaluationContext(ClientModel, AccessToken) in ClientPermissionsV2 is defined but never called anywhere in the class, making it unreachable dead code": 0.6648985147476196}